From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Open Arc Authors <dev@openarc.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:53:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: embedder: extensions

Plan task C14: //chrome's extension system on the embedder's profiles,
behind OACProfile.extensions (OACExtensions.h):

- installedExtensions / actionsForTab: the profile's user-facing extensions
  (no component extensions) and, per tab, each toolbar action's icon (PNG,
  16 pt at 2x; the placeholder letter until the default icon loaded, which an
  IconImage observer reports), badge, title, enabled state and popup. These
  are what the shell's Site Control Center shows in its "Extensions" section.
- runActionOfExtension:onTab: ExtensionActionRunner::RunAction (activeTab,
  then action.onClicked or the popup), as a click on Chrome's toolbar button.
  A popup is an ExtensionViewHost of type popup (OACExtensionPopup) whose
  WebContents view the shell hosts in its own bubble; auto-resize within
  Chrome's popup limits, load and close (window.close(), Escape) reach the
  shell through OACExtensionPopupDelegate. One popup at a time per profile.
- Install confirmations: ExtensionInstallPrompt's embedder dialog (the
  previous patch) becomes an OACExtensionInstallRequest for the profile's
  delegate, with the asking tab (the Web Store page), Chromium's title,
  button labels and permission warnings. installFromWebStoreWithIdentifier:
  uses Chrome's WebstoreInstallWithPrompt.
- loadUnpackedFromURL: UnpackedInstaller, with developer mode turned on
  (Chromium disables unpacked extensions without it).
- setEnabled / uninstall through ExtensionRegistrar.
- chrome.tabs.query lists the bridge's tabs (the previous patch's list).
